025-26.\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n \n\nStudy Scheme\n\n\nLearning Outcomes\n \n\n\t\n\n1.          Major Programme:\n\nUpon programme completion, graduates will have acquired the ability to:\n\n(1)      demonstrate mastery of fundamental concepts involved in meeting the health and social care needs of the aging population, including\n\n- the biological, physical, psychological, and social aspects of ageing;\n\n- successful aging;\n\n- chronic disease management for older people;\n\n- community/residential care service planning;\n\n- interdisciplinary aged care service planning, administration, coordination, and delivery; (K)\n\n(2)      demonstrate the skills needed in assessing and delivering evidence-based care for older people in the community, rehabilitative, and residential care settings; (K/S)\n\n(3)      plan and coordinate aged care services within and across these settings; (K/S)\n\n(4)      critically evaluate the impacts of the changing health care, social, and cultural contexts and contemporary policies on decision-making for aged care service planning, coordination, evaluation, and re-engineering; (K/V)\n\n(5)      assess, interpret, and apply innovative health and social care models in evaluating and re-engineering aged care services within and across the community, rehabilitative and residential care settings; (K/S/V)\n\n(6)      work effectively with other professionals involved in aged care service provision and apply the interdisciplinary collaborative care model in planning and coordinating these services; (K/S/V)\n\n(7)       demonstrate effective communication and interpersonal skills in dealing with older people, their caregivers and families, and other professionals involved in the provision of aged care services; (K/S/V)\n\n(8)       demonstrate the ability to advocate best practices and assume a leadership role in coordinating and fostering interprofessional practice; (K/S/V)\n\n(9)       drive social innovation in practice and lead innovation in aged care; (K/S/V)\n\n(10)  exhibit professionalism in practice and adhere to legal and ethical standards of aged care; (K/S)\n\n(11)  demonstrate mastery of research skills and utilise research evidence in the provision of aged care services; (K/S) and\n\n(12)  display personal and social responsibility and engage in lifelong learning and personal development. (V)\n\n \n\nK = Knowledge outcomes       S = Skills outcomes       V = Values and attitudes outcomes\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n\n"
